Note on the focused-run shape (the package's own script is the only one that works): `vitest run --root . src/...` from packages/mcp finds ZERO tests, because the repo config's include is `packages/**/*.test.ts`. The working shape is `--root ../..` with repo-relative paths.

Cases, stdio (packages/mcp/src/stdio/stdio-server.test.ts):
- filters to exactly the allowlisted kinds, with expected NAMES DERIVED by mapping the input through the production `toolLabelForKind` — never a hand-pinned roster, so task-c52d25a4 growing the daemon's wired set cannot redden this;
- the filtered list is strictly SHORTER than STDIO_TOOL_ENTRIES, so a no-op "filter" that returns everything fails;
- unknown kind refuses AT CONSTRUCTION: asserts `created === false`, the exact code MCP_TOOL_ALLOWLIST_UNKNOWN_KIND, the offending kind by name, and that the message does NOT name the innocent sibling kind;
- empty allowlist refuses with its own code MCP_TOOL_ALLOWLIST_EMPTY (an MCP server advertising zero tools is a misconfiguration, per the plan's decision);
- no-allowlist arm asserts the advertised array equals the generated entries' {description, inputSchema, name} exactly, not just the length.

Cases, HTTP (packages/mcp/src/http/http-parity.test.ts): the same allowlist over `createHttpMcpAdapter` yields the same names as stdio (both compared against the derived list AND against each other); without an allowlist both transports advertise the full generated set; an unknown kind refuses at ADAPTER construction with the same stable code. That last one forces eager validation — the HTTP server object is only built when a session opens, so a lazily-validated allowlist would refuse at first request instead of at construction.

Generation (stdio-tool-schemas.ts:199-206) is untouched, so stdio-schemas.test.ts's "covers every command and query kind exactly once" pin needs no edit and stays valid.
